.TH IMPROV-TUI 1 "" "improv" "Improv Manual"
.SH NAME
improv\-tui \- terminal pivot viewer and editor for Improv models
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBimprov\-tui\fR <model>
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B improv-tui
shows one measure of a model as a pivot grid in the terminal: one category
down the rows, one across the columns, the rest as pages. Input cells are
edited in place; derived measures recompute incrementally as you type.
Each change is saved as it is made, writing only what changed, so closing
the terminal loses nothing. If a save fails (a full disk, another program
saved the model), the status box's title says
.B not saved
and the status line says why; the edits stay in the session.
.PP
A model is a store file made by
.BR improv (1),
or a Postgres model URL,
.BI postgres:// user @ host / db ?model= name\fR.
A new file, or a model with nothing in it, opens empty: build it with
.BR c ,
.BR n " and"
.BR = .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fImodel\fR>
The model: a store file (a new one opens empty), or postgres://USER@HOST/DB?model=NAME
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B arrows\fR, mouse click
Move the cell cursor.
.TP
.B Shift+arrows
Select a range; its sum shows in the status line.
.TP
.BR e ", " Enter
Edit the selected input cell. On a derived measure,
.B e
edits its formula, shown as it was typed
.RB ( "Price * Quantity" ;
a formula the symbolic form cannot spell shows in controlled English,
.BR "Price times Quantity" ),
and takes either form. Enter only says the cell is computed. A formula that would leave the measure one value over no
categories, such as
.BR 5 ,
needs a second Enter. A cell's old value shows selected: the first key
typed replaces it, and Left, Right, Home, End or Backspace first edit it in
place. A number cell takes
.BR 1500 ,
.BR \-3.5 ,
.B 1,500.25
and
.B $1,500
(a leading dollar, euro, pound or yen sign; with
.BR IMPROV_LOCALE=de ,
.B 1.500,25
and
.BR \(Eu1.500 );
.B 1,50
is refused, not guessed. Enter commits (an empty edit clears the cell), Esc cancels; on an
error the edit
stays open with the message under it. A formula that does not parse has
the offending token underlined in red, a
.B ^~~~
marker under it, the message, and a hint for the common mistakes: the
closest names to a misspelled one, a function's parameters when it got the
wrong number of arguments, the parenthesis left open. Left/Right, Home/End,
Backspace and Delete edit at the caret.
.TP
.BR 0 \(en 9 ", " - ", " .
Start editing the selected input cell with that key as its new value.
.TP
.B Tab \fR(in a formula)
Complete the name before the caret: a function (as
.IB NAME (\fR),
a measure or a category. One match completes; several extend to their
common prefix and list on the status line, and each further Tab puts the
next one in. While the caret is inside a call the status line shows its
signature, the current argument marked
.BR \(fopv\(fc ,
and at the end of the line the parameters still to type follow the caret,
dimmed.
.TP
.BR Tab ", " m
Show the next measure.
.TP
.B p
Pivot: rotate the axis order.
.TP
.BR [ " and " ]
Page through the page dimensions.
.TP
.BR f " / " F
Hide the cursor row's item / clear all filters.
.TP
.B S
Save the current layout as a view: type its name, or press Enter for the
one offered
.RB ( "view 1" ,
.BR "view 2" ,
\&...). A name in use is refused.
.TP
.B v
Cycle through the saved views.
.TP
.B V
Rename or delete a saved view:
.IR Old " = " New
renames one,
.BI \- Name
deletes it.
.TP
.BR I " / " E
Import a CSV into a new measure / export the shown measure (a prompt opens).
.TP
.B c
Add a category and its items (each prompt shows its syntax, dimmed, until
you type). Type
.I Name
or
.IR Name ": " item ", " item ", .\|.\|.;"
on an existing category it adds the items it does not have yet. A
category may not take a measure's or a LAMBDA's name, nor a measure a
category's: formulas name both.
.TP
.B n
Add a number input measure and show it. Type
.I Name
(a single value) or
.IR Name ": " Category ", " Category ", .\|.\|.,"
the categories it ranges over: the first two are the grid's rows and
columns, the rest pages.
.TP
.B r
Rename a category, item or measure: type
.IR Old " = " New .
An item is
.I Item
when one category has it, else
.IR Category . Item .
Formulas hold what they read, not its name, so they follow. A category,
a measure and a LAMBDA may not share a name, nor two items of a category.
.TP
.B D
Delete a category, item or measure: type its name. A measure a formula
reads, or a category a measure ranges over or a formula names, is refused
with the formulas named. An item takes its cells, and a measure its cells
and its saved views. One
.B u
brings it all back.
.TP
.B =
Define: a line that takes what
.B improv define
takes.
.B Revenue = Price * Quantity
adds a derived measure, or gives an existing one a new formula;
.B Margin = LAMBDA(p, q, p - q)
defines a named LAMBDA that formulas then call as
.BR Margin(Price,\ 1) .
Tab completes, and errors are located, as in a formula edit.
.TP
.B #
Set the shown measure's number format: type
.B general
or a count of decimals, 0 to 15, then
.B grouped
for thousands separators
.RB ( 2 ,
.BR "0 grouped" ,
.BR "general grouped" ).
The prompt shows the format now; Enter on an empty line keeps it.
Decimals round half away from zero, the separators follow
.BR IMPROV_LOCALE ,
and the values are untouched: an edit starts from the value as typed.
One undo step; saved with the model.
.TP
.B w
Save now: retry a save that failed.
.TP
.B R
Revert to the saved model, dropping this session's unsaved edits and its
undo history. Use it after a save conflict, when another writer changed
the model. With edits or history to lose it says what goes, and a second
.B R
reverts; any other key keeps them.
.TP
.B u
Undo the last change to the model: a cell, a formula, an import, a
rename or delete, a saved view. Up to 50 changes are kept.
.TP
.B Ctrl+R
Redo the last change
.B u
undid. A new change drops what was undone.
.TP
.BR ? ", " F1
Open the list of every key (the status box shows the common ones on one
line) and the function help: type to search the built-in functions, Up/Down and
PgUp/PgDn move through the results, and the selected function's signature,
category, aliases and description show below them. Enter inserts
.IB NAME (
into the cell being edited (F1 works while editing); Esc closes.
.TP
.B q
Quit and save.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B IMPROV_LOCALE
The locale (else the OS locale): the decimal and thousands separators a
number cell takes and a number format writes,
.B 1,234.50
in English and
.B 1.234,50
for
.BR de .
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
improv-tui sample.db
improv-tui new.db   # empty: c, n, e and = build it, w saves
improv-tui 'postgres://me@127.0.0.1/sales?sslmode=disable&model=plan'
.fi
